{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/399871-moonsilver-tats-or-why-did-the-lunars-get-shafted","id":399871,"title":"Moonsilver Tats (or, Why Did The Lunars Get Shafted)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T20:22:26-08:00","id":399871,"title":"Moonsilver Tats (or, Why Did The Lunars Get Shafted)","content":"At risk of beating a dead horse\u2014what's up with them? From what I've read (all 2E stuff, mind) the Lunars are so diminished that a band of Freedom Stone denizens revamped everything from their chargen to most of their charms. And Luna's Glories of the Most High book explicitly says that parts of sorcery, martial arts, artifacts, thaumaturgy, etc., are off-limits to Lunars because of the tattoos, which are apparently good enough to block out positive effects that the Lunar enacts but not good enough to protect them from mental or spiritual warping. Most of their charms, from what I've seen, revolve around their bodies (moving in this special way, doing this feat of strength, having these super-sharp claws all come to mind.) And of course 90% of them are animal-themed, because the Solars have everything sun-themed and the Terrestrials have everything dragon-themed oh wait (and to forestall 'did you look in the books' yes I have and they seem less tunnel-visioned on those themes even if only slightly.) Despite them being the only other kind of Exalts in Creation for hundreds of years, the Lunars are dominated by these crazy Elders and their useless, do-nothing factions that have... established a bunch of ragtag societies? Let Creation go to hell so the Solars can save the day with their magic sparkly sun powers? And to top it all off, Lytek apparently didn't touch them or work on their Great Curse or the alleged Wyld taint even though he's had pretty much nothing else to do since the Usurpation. They have very few decent unique artifacts and a remarkably low number of hearthstones for people who should be masters of establishing bastions in the wilderness. Again, Lunars are rather restricted by their tattoos\u2014how on earth did they break the castes, anyway? What explanation was there for them suddenly not settling themselves post-Usurpation? Wyld, yes, but shards of power from a debatably mad, fluid god(dess) who already walks the Wyld when (s)he's not playing the Games looking for Gaia. And you can't tell me that the Lunars suddenly lost all knowledge of stabilizing the Wyld when they fled there or didn't find a way to hide in Creation. The tattoos protect them primarily from shaping in a place they don't need to visit and from their own powers hurting them like exactly no other splat's powers do. Their powers are such that I was dumbstruck upon finding Ink Monkey charms that had the Lunars doing super-magical stuff like walking on moonlight and inflicting nightmares\u2014y'know, moon-and-madness stuff that fits Luna instead of them being only shapeshifters skilled with their bodies. Instead of being the Stewards and slightly-less-than equals of the Solars, it's hard to imagine how these guys ever functioned. Don't even get me started on their castes again. Hell, the Solars had their Exaltations imprisoned after being attached to a bunch of nutjobs and left alone for centuries and then broken into by the Yozis/Neverborn and they came out with all of their castes!<br /> <br /> This is a pretty open-ended topic. Opinions, fixes, explanations, all are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":